ous turn of QQQ+3. Since KKK is higher than QQQ, they are very likely to pass again unless they were holding back a Bomb or 2s. This allows me to maintain the initiative (the "lead").\n\nReason:\nThe hand contains too many unconnected small singles (4, 5, 6, 9, J). The most effective way to reduce the card count is to attach a single to the strong KKK triplet. KKK is a top-tier rank (beaten only by 222 or Bombs since I hold AA), making it a very safe play to regain or keep control. Opponents already showed weakness by passing on QQQ, so KKK is statistically likely to win the trick.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♦4", "♠K", "♥K", "♣K"]}'}
